<title>JAPAN: Yasuda Mutual reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Yasuda Mutual reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yasuda Mutual Life Insurance Co has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans		9.7	     42.8</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  38.7		4.8</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	    5.4		5.5</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients     1.4		1.4</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    55.2	     54.5</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
